Thought this might be of interest to the group:

NEMONIX Launches Custom Engineering Services and VAX HotLine Site Support

Targets Operators of America's 175,000 VAX Computers Still in Operation

HOLLISTON, Mass. -- June 28, 2004 -- In a move to help prolong the lives of
thousands of mission-critical legacy computers and minimize the impact of
unscheduled downtime, NEMONIX(TM) Engineering, Inc. today launched the VAX
HotLine(TM) site support and a separate custom engineering services program
to meet a growing demand for hardware support, upgrades, replacements and
other enhancements for VAX computers. NEMONIX is the world's only provider
of a wide range of VAX memory, storage, networking, acceleration and adaptor
hardware upgrades.

As companies continue to struggle with limited IT budgets, NEMONIX is
targeting operators of the nearly 175,000 VAX machines still in operation in
the United States alone -- computers that continue to power critical
operations for companies across a multitude of industries. Replacement parts
for these systems have become more and more difficult to find, and many have
been discontinued. Finding qualified service technicians who can respond
quickly to issues has also become more challenging. Regardless of a
company's long-term data migration strategy, when a hardware component that
powers a critical function fails, the downtime can quickly become costly.

The newly-launched VAX HotLine will support a company's entire site,
regardless of the number of registered VAX computers. The HotLine's license
permits any individual calling from a registered VAX installation to receive
support through the program. Within two hours, a qualified VAX technician
will be made available to address any hardware issues the client is facing.
The program offers extended support hours up to 24x7. It is the only VAX
support program of its kind, and designed to permit flexible, fast response
to both critical and routine support needs. Companies can purchase support
in increments of 10, 20 and 40 hours, and purchased time blocks expire
after one year.

Additionally, through the new custom engineering services program announced
today, NEMONIX customers can work with the company's engineering staff to
design and manufacture custom components to replace or prepare for the i
eventual replacement of failed parts. The company's staff of engineers and
technicians is considered to be one of the largest concentrations of VAX
expertise in the nation, and is able to turn around production replacement
parts at an accelerated pace.

"With these two new services services, NEMONIX extends a 20-year track
record serving the needs of VAX users, providing products and services that
help maintain critical operations and maximize legacy technology
investments," said Beth Bumbarger, senior partner and director of marketing
at NEMONIX. "Our current engineering capabilities let us provide an
extraordinary level of custom development services and support to the
extended VAX community. We are pleased to be able to announce these
capabilities, and we look forward to helping our customers meet the
engineering challenges facing today's enterprise computing world."

The company's custom engineering services have already been tested. Said
Bumbarger: "Our depot-level repair center was approached by a customer
looking to replace a highly specialized VAX component that was not in our
product catalog, and we were able to quickly re-engineer and manufacture
the component to help this customer resume operations."

NEMONIX Engineering will be on hand at HP World 2004 in Chicago to
demonstrate its technology capabilities as an HP DSPP partner.

About NEMONIX Engineering
NEMONIX Engineering helps companies maximize their legacy technology
investments. NEMONIX is the world\x92s only provider of a wide range of
VAX memory, storage, networking, acceleration and adaptor hardware
upgrades. It is also a leading depot-level repair center for everything
from PDP-11s to VAXs, Alphas and PCs. For more than 20 years, NEMONIX
has partnered with companies like Digital, Compaq and HP to provide
support for the widest range of high-capacity technology platforms. The
company offers 24x7 support to meet the real-time, mission-critical
demands placed on these powerful minicomputers. NEMONIX Engineering is
the exclusive distributor of Data Wizard on the OpenVMS platform, a
powerful data integration and migration tool that can extend the
lifetime of critical legacy applications and ensure a smooth transition
when the time comes to upgrade or replace systems. NEMONIX offers
custom engineering services that can help companies replace hard-to-
find and discontinued components and systems. For more information on
NEMONIX, visit the company's website at www.nemonixengineering.com or
call 1-800-435-8650.

