If the in-wall cat-5 wiring is 'standard', you can use a BN24H-xx and 
BN24J-xx wire pair to connect to an RJ45-port DECserver, like a 90TL or 
a 90M.  BN24's have an RJ45 plug at one end, MMJ on the other.  The 'J' 
and 'H' indicate straight through and crossover (though I do not know 
which is which...).  You can use either cable for the terminal to 
walljack connection, and the other for patch panel to DECserver. the -xx 
generally indicates the length.



VT510 -- BN24J -- jack -- wiring -- patch panel -- BN24H -- DS90M

   or

VT510 -- BN24H -- jack -- wiring -- patch panel -- BN24J -- DS90M


If you have a DECserver with MMJ connectors, then you still use one of 
the BN24 cables (the straight through one, sorry, not sure of the 
letter), and a standard MMJ-MMJ (BC16???) cable from patch panel to 
DECserver.  I have no info on digi products.

Rich
