Looking for DEC hardware in Sweden, Denmark, the Netherlands, Belgium 
and England.  Feel free to forward this to anyone who might be 
interested.

I will be in England for a few days in August.  As I will be out of
contact with cyberspace for almost all of July, I'm posting this now and
of course need feedback by the end of June.

The last two weeks in July I will be in Sweden.  Travel plans aren't 
firm yet, so if you have something I might want, let me know!  I'll be 
passing through Denmark on the way to Sweden; again, travel plans are 
not yet firm.

For details on England, the Netherlands and Belgium, see the end of this 
post.

I'm looking for DEC hardware.  I have "enough" in some sense, but I do
need replacement parts for things which fail etc.  Of course, I might
decide I need to increase the size of my cluster at some point.  In any
case, anything I collect will be used, will be waiting to be used or, if
I really don't need it anymore, will go to a good home.

Here's what I'm looking for:

"Computers": any desktop or "minitower" ALPHA, any desktop VAX or
VAXstation 4000

memory: while it's doubtful that someone would have bare memory, I'm
interested if I have a system it will work in

hard disks: any SBB disk 1GB or larger (RZ26, RZ28, RZ29)---9-GB or
18-GB SBB disks would be especially welcome, "internal" disks 1GB or
larger, especially 9GB

CD-ROM drives

CD-ROM drives and disks should be SCSI, though DSSI might be interesting 
if 1 GB or more

colour monitors: especially the somewhat older ones which have BNC 
connectors (RBG) for the monitor and three round plugs for the graphics 
card (the plugs are smaller than BNC connectors, but much larger than 
the pins in other plugs)

cables: SCSI, MMJ serial cables

switches, hubs, repeaters etc

paper documentation: VMS 7.x 

Essentially, I am looking for used equipment which is no longer needed 
which the owner/maintainer would like to see go to a good home rather 
than be scrapped.  However, for some things I might be willing to pay a 
small fee.  I also have an ALPHAstation 2000 and an ALPHAstation 2100.
I'm not sure if I want to keep them (they are nice machines, and I 
actually have room for them, but I am concerned about power consumption, 
even if they don't consume the presumably maximum values printed on the 
housing; if I can ever justify the cost of the power, I can justify the 
cost of buying newer, faster, less power-hungry hardware), though if I 
do I can use them occasionally (say, as temporary replacements) even if 
I don't keep them switched on all the time.  However, if someone is 
looking for such a machine, I would be willing to trade it for some of 
the above stuff and/or sell it for a reasonable fee (to cover my costs 
in buying them and/or collecting them).

I can also offer in trade a couple of SCSI CD-ROM drives which only do 
2048-byte sectors (i.e. they won't work with VMS).

I will arrive in Kent on Tuesday 10 August, be in the Manchester area on 
Wednesday 11 August and in Oxfordshire Thursday--Saturday 12--14 August.
Obviously, I will make the corresponding journeys, but could go as far 
out of the way as time permits.  I will be heading back Sunday, but will 
have very little time, though it might be possible to collect something 
early Sunday morning if it is between Oxfordshire and Kent.  On the way 
there, I will be passing through the Netherlands and the western part of 
Belgium, so would be interested in collecting stuff there on Sunday 8 
August or possibly Monday 9 August.

Please email me if you can offer me something!



